{
  "dom_id": "step-e13757",
  "name": "Example: Raising a Number to the First Power",
  "problem": "Find the value of $6^1.$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, ${\\color{blue}6}^{\\color{red}1}$ is in exponent form. The base is $\\color{blue}6$ and the exponent is ${\\color{red}1}.$ \n\nThis means that $\\color{blue}6$ is taken as a factor only once. Therefore,\n\n$$\n6^1 = 6.\n$$",
